 practice block and useful reflection at a time.</p><a class="action" href="pathway-index.html">Map a pathway<span>↗</span></a></div><figure><img src="assets/images/hero.png" alt="Modular paper learning landscape with notebooks, pathways and illuminated knowledge nodes"><figcaption><span>ACTIVE MAP</span><b>FOUNDATION → PRACTICE → APPLICATION</b></figcaption></figure><div class="map-coordinates"><span>A1</span><span>B4</span><span>C7</span><span>D2</span></div></section>
<section class="subject-ribbon" id="home-02"><div><span>READING</span><span>REASONING</span><span>WRITING</span><span>SCIENCE</span><span>DIGITAL SKILLS</span><span>STUDY METHOD</span><span>READING</span><span>REASONING</span></div></section>
<section class="matrix-builder" id="home-03"><header><p class="label">03 / SKILL MATRIX</p><h2>See what is strong.<br>Choose what moves next.</h2><p>A practical matrix separates confidence from evidence. Select a cell to inspect the next useful action.</p></header><div class="matrix-tool"><div class="matrix-labels"><span>FOUNDATION</span><span>PRACTICE</span><span>TRANSFER</span><span>REFLECTION</span></div><div class="matrix-cells" role="group" aria-label="Interactive learning matrix"><button data-cell="1" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 1"><i></i><b>01</b></button><button data-cell="2" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 2"><i></i><b>02</b></button><button data-cell="3" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 3"><i></i><b>03</b></button><button data-cell="4" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 4"><i></i><b>04</b></button><button data-cell="5" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 5"><i></i><b>05</b></button><button data-cell="6" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 6"><i></i><b>06</b></button><button data-cell="7" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 7"><i></i><b>07</b></button><button data-cell="8" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 8"><i></i><b>08</b></button><button data-cell="9" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 9"><i></i><b>09</b></button><button data-cell="10" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 10"><i></i><b>10</b></button><button data-cell="11" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 11"><i></i><b>11</b></button><button data-cell="12" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 12"><i></i><b>12</b></button><button data-cell="13" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 13"><i></i><b>13</b></button><button data-cell="14" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 14"><i></i><b>14</b></button><button data-cell="15" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 15"><i></i><b>15</b></button><button data-cell="16" aria-label="Learning matrix cell 16"><i></i><b>16</b></button></div><aside><small>NEXT MOVE</small><b data-matrix-title>RETRIEVE WITHOUT NOTES</b><p data-matrix-copy>Close the source and write the three ideas you can explain from memory.</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="lesson-staircase" id="home-04"><div class="stair-copy"><p class="label">04 / LESSON STAIRCASE</p><h2>Build difficulty in useful steps.</h2><p class="lead">Progress is easier to read when each stage asks for a slightly more demanding use of the same idea.</p></div><ol><li><b>01</b><div><h3>Recognise</h3><p>Identify the idea and distinguish it from nearby concepts.</p></div></li><li><b>02</b><div><h3>Recall</h3><p>Bring the key structure back without looking at the source.</p></div></li><li><b>03</b><div><h3>Explain</h3><p>Describe the idea in your own words with a clear example.</p></div></li><li><b>04</b><div><h3>Apply</h3><p>Use the idea in a new question, task or realistic situation.</p></div></li></ol></section>
<section class="focus-clock" id="home-05"><div class="clock-face" data-clock><div class="clock-core"><span data-minutes>25</span><small>MINUTES</small></div><i class="clock-hand"></i><button type="button" data-time="15">15</button><button type="button" data-time="25" class="active">25</button><button type="button" data-time="40">40</button></div><div class="clock-copy"><p class="label">05 / FOCUS CLOCK</p><h2>Give attention a clear boundary.</h2><p class="lead">Choose a realistic block, define one visible outcome, remove competing tabs and stop long enough to record what remains unfinished.</p><ul><li><b>START</b><span>Write the outcome in one sentence.</span></li><li><b>WORK</b><span>Keep one source and one task visible.</span></li><li><b>STOP</b><span>Mark the exact place to resume.</span></li></ul></div></section>
<section class="learning-loop" id="home-06"><figure><img src="assets/images/study.png" alt="Overhead collaborative study table with concept cards, notebooks and a progress grid"></figure><div><p class="label">06 / THE LEARNING LOOP</p><h2>Study becomes useful when it returns.</h2><p class="lead">Read to build a first model, retrieve to expose gaps, practise to strengthen decisions, and reflect to improve the next session.</p><div class="loop-track"><span>01<br><b>INPUT</b></span><span>02<br><b>RECALL</b></span><span>03<br><b>PRACTICE</b></span><span>04<br><b>REVIEW</b></span></div><a class="action dark" href="learning-method.html">Explore the method<span>↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="resource-shelves" id="home-07"><header><p class="label">07 / RESOURCE SHELVES</p><h2>Keep materials small enough to use.</h2></header><div class="shelves"><article><span>01</span><h3>Concept card</h3><p>One question on the front; a short explanation and example on the back.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Error log</h3><p>A brief record of what went wrong, why it happened and the correction.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Practice set</h3><p>A focused group of questions that tests one skill at varied difficulty.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Weekly map</h3><p>Three priorities, realistic time blocks and one planned review point.</p></article></div></section>
